From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lxc: copy host permissions on non-Treble hosts too

setup_host_perms() copies the host's NFC and consumer-IR feature
declarations into /var/lib/waydroid/host-permissions, which is bind
mounted over /vendor/etc/host-permissions in the container. It bails out
first unless ro.treble.enabled is "true".

That gate is wrong for a Halium host. The container gets the host's
/vendor bind mounted as vendor_extra regardless of Treble, so the HAL is
visible to Android whether or not the feature XML was copied. When the
two disagree, system_server does not degrade - it throws:

  FATAL EXCEPTION IN SYSTEM PROCESS: main
  java.lang.RuntimeException: IR HAL present, but FEATURE_CONSUMER_IR is
      not set!
      at com.android.server.ConsumerIrService.<init>(ConsumerIrService.java:54)
      at com.android.server.SystemServer.startOtherServices(SystemServer.java:1152)

and Android crash-loops every five seconds, never reaching
sys.boot_completed.

Reproduced on a Xiaomi Mi A1 (tissot) running LuneOS on Halium 9, which
has an IR blaster: ro.treble.enabled is "false", so host-permissions
stayed empty while /vendor/etc/permissions/android.hardware.consumerir.xml
and /vendor/lib64/hw/consumerir.default.so were both present.

Dropping the gate is safe. Every entry in copy_list is already guarded by
its own os.path.exists() or glob(), so on a host that genuinely has
neither HAL the function still copies nothing - it just no longer decides
that in advance from an unrelated property. The sku lookup keeps working
as before; on a non-Treble host ro.boot.product.hardware.sku is empty and
that branch is skipped by the existing check.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/helpers/lxc.py | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

--- a/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -346,10 +346,6 @@ def setup_host_perms(args):
     if not os.path.exists(tools.config.defaults["host_perms"]):
         os.mkdir(tools.config.defaults["host_perms"])

-    treble = tools.helpers.props.host_get(args, "ro.treble.enabled")
-    if treble != "true":
-        return
-
     sku = tools.helpers.props.host_get(args, "ro.boot.product.hardware.sku")
     copy_list = []
     copy_list.extend(
